{"nodes": [{"id": "readme_open4wd_pinning", "label": "Open4WD Pinning Public Template", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Public template (\u516c\u7248) for Open4WD pinning nodes: a node keeps ledger, checkpoints, cold match partitions and UGC according to operator policy, and may optionally offer bootstrap, controlled UGC pin/unpin, DMCA and transparency capabilities. The project is still in development and the main game is not yet public; the repo is a reviewable, self-deployable service template, not an officially operated node. The public repo itself does not deploy, holds no secrets, and does not designate or pre-select any pinning endpoint."}, {"id": "readme_operator_fork_policy", "label": "Operator Fork Policy", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Because the public template stays neutral (no deployment, no secrets, no pre-selected endpoint), each operator fork must decide its own capacity, public capabilities, legal-compliance responsibility and availability policy. Operator-owned inputs such as config/config.yaml and CLUSTER_SECRET (openssl rand -hex 32) are created by the operator and never shipped in the template."}, {"id": "readme_quick_start", "label": "Pinning Node Quick Start", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Shortest success path kept in the root README. Prerequisites: Node.js 24, pnpm 11, Docker Compose, OpenSSL. Steps: clone, pnpm install --frozen-lockfile, copy config/config.example.yaml to config/config.yaml, fill at least the receipt ledger_db_address and genesis_timestamp, set the OpenSSL output as CLUSTER_SECRET, docker compose -f deploy/docker/docker-compose.yml up -d, then pnpm exec tsx scripts/smoke.ts http://127.0.0.1:8000 (local smoke checks GET /stats and a non-empty node_id)."}, {"id": "readme_strict_smoke_gate", "label": "Strict Deployment Smoke Gate", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Production deployments additionally run scripts/smoke.ts --strict against the public URL (e.g. https://pin.example.org). Strict mode requires ipfs_cluster_peers >= 1 and available_space_bytes > 0 on top of the basic GET /stats + node_id check, so a node without a cluster peer or without free space fails the gate."}, {"id": "readme_deployment_authority", "label": "Open4WD Specs Pinning Deployment Authority", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": "https://github.com/xjustloveux/open-4wd-specs/blob/master/%E9%83%A8%E7%BD%B2%E8%B3%87%E8%A8%8A/open-4wd-pinning.md", "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Single-source-of-truth rule: the root README keeps only the shortest success path; full configuration values, genesis/rebirth, DMCA, backup, Kubernetes workflow and operator responsibilities are authoritative in open-4wd-specs \u90e8\u7f72\u8cc7\u8a0a/open-4wd-pinning.md. Environment variables and defaults are deliberately not duplicated as a second table in the README. In-repo manuals and templates: deploy/sizing/README.md, deploy/monitoring/README.md, deploy/docker/docker-compose.yml, deploy/k8s/, config/config.example.yaml, dmca/openapi.ts."}, {"id": "readme_explicit_peering_policy", "label": "Explicit-Peering-Only Kubo Policy", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The public-template Kubo uses only explicit Peering and does not join the public DHT, because enabling public routing lets generic block serving bypass the root-scoped UGC policy. An operator who turns on public routing must re-measure capacity and disclose the privacy, legal-compliance and content-serving boundaries."}, {"id": "readme_ledger_genesis_ceremony", "label": "One-Time Ledger Genesis Ceremony", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Ledger genesis is a one-time ceremony and is not auto-created by the regular service. Before running it, per Specs \u00a73.4, prepare a dedicated data directory, a stable identity, the governance signer set, the release commit and the external receipt path; the receipt (ledger_db_address, genesis_timestamp) is what config.yaml later consumes."}, {"id": "readme_vendored_protocol_manifest", "label": "Vendored Protocol Closure Manifest", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "core/vendor/ is synchronized from the main project and locked by MANIFEST.json (dependency closure + SHA-256); it must never be hand-edited. After a local sync run pnpm check:vendor:local; run pnpm check:vendor only when the full release gate is needed."}, {"id": "readme_manual_deploy_opt_in", "label": "Manual Deployment Opt-In", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The public deploy workflow only accepts manual opt-in from operator forks and is not a dependency of CI, build or image publish. This keeps the template itself non-deploying while letting forks deploy deliberately."}, {"id": "readme_dmca_openapi_runtime_contract", "label": "DMCA OpenAPI Runtime Contract", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "dmca/openapi.ts is the DMCA OpenAPI generator; the runtime contract is served by the node at GET /api/dmca/openapi.json. Full DMCA operating procedure is defined in the Specs deployment authority."}, {"id": "readme_policy_aware_retrieval", "label": "Policy-Aware Retrieval (Root-Scoped UGC Policy)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A pinning node keeps ledger, checkpoints, cold match partitions and UGC according to operator policy and serves UGC under a root-scoped policy (core/ provider policy). Optional capabilities (bootstrap, controlled UGC pin/unpin, DMCA, transparency) are operator choices, not guarantees; generic public block serving would bypass this root-scoped policy."}, {"id": "readme_verification_chain", "label": "Pinning Verification Chain", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Local verification commands: pnpm test, pnpm test:integration, pnpm e2e, pnpm check:vendor:local, pnpm check:comments:self-test, pnpm check:comments. Integration may be skipped locally without Docker; official CI runs it against real Kubo/Cluster."}, {"id": "readme_open4wd_main_repository", "label": "Open4WD Main Repository", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": "https://github.com/xjustloveux/open-4wd", "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "readme_open4wd_specs_repository", "label": "Open4WD Specs Repository", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": "https://github.com/xjustloveux/open-4wd-specs", "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "readme_signaling_template", "label": "Open4WD Signaling Template", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": "https://github.com/xjustloveux/open-4wd-signaling", "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "readme_turn_template", "label": "Open4WD TURN Template", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": "https://github.com/xjustloveux/open-4wd-turn", "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "readme_open4wd_security_policy", "label": "Open4WD Security Policy", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": "https://github.com/xjustloveux/open-4wd/security/policy", "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Security vulnerabilities must be reported privately through the main repository's GitHub security policy rather than disclosed publicly; ordinary contributions go through GitHub Issues / Pull Requests."}, {"id": "readme_third_party_notices", "label": "Third-Party MIT Notices (THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md)", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Code adapted from third-party MIT-licensed projects keeps its original copyright and license notices in THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md, alongside the repo's own MIT LICENSE."}, {"id": "readme_mit_license", "label": "MIT License", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}], "edges": [{"source": "readme_open4wd_pinning", "target": "readme_operator_fork_policy", "relation": "conceptually_related_to", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "readme_open4wd_pinning", "target": "readme_quick_start", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "co